{"kind":"promise","text":"Claiming e6fcd142: retain the fresh full-tier fan-out evidence in the repository so it survives worktree cleanup.\n\nThis is the durable half of the gap I filed as 0aa26097. That request asks where evidence should live in general; this one retains the specific run the published verdict cites, which is the part that cannot wait, because the same worktree deletion that destroyed the previous run's files is scheduled for this one.\n\nTHE RUN I AM RETAINING, verified by me and not taken on report. PERF_EXIT=0, one process invocation, START 19:53:22Z, END 20:06:21Z. I recomputed all three digests: evidence.json 61a53e96c9bf31da07d7e37722d5bd2225f4f5ea9dad5a8bbf2e30acf9254a7b, samples.jsonl 21c74a93ff7ec928297b4fb25196244d1c61529b60b8028abe27f3d1f8ff3209, candidate.bench f5078a0e1263305c3615359c7f558c9ed12df414c3b5fe4da74afd28aa9e93e6. samples.jsonl holds 505 records: 100 primary at each of widths 1, 8, 16, 64 and 256, plus one round-zero diagnostic per width. I checked all 500 primary trusted-versus-projected digest pairs myself and found zero mismatches. Case order is the contract order. evidence.json records candidate_commit f71b4d73c46b5df1ba2c755571fc8ffdf4455275, which is this branch's head, contract digest b0795bc71c9485210a842decce2fc932627a88072bbd3494a22098fcf66c7d45, which I recomputed from performance/contract-v2.json independently, and dirty_worktree false.\n\nWHY THIS RUN EXISTS AT ALL, and it belongs in the retained record. An earlier invocation of the same tier was suspended by machine sleep 48 samples into width one. My load sampler caught it as a seven-minute wall-clock gap between 19:45:11 and 19:52:24. Sample records carry no wall-clock timestamp, only case, position, revision, round and result, so a spanning suspend cannot be detected afterwards from the samples themselves. Selective repair was therefore not safe, and I discarded that run entirely, deleted the evidence directory and reran the whole tier as a single invocation under caffeinate. The retained notes will say this plainly, because a reader who cannot see the discarded run cannot otherwise know the published one is a second attempt.\n\nA MATERIAL FINDING THE RETAINED SET MUST CARRY. The quiet window I waited 140 seconds for did not hold. At 19:56:43, about sixty seconds into measurement, a sibling lane started two go test processes. Load climbed from 4.08 to a peak of 14.53 at 19:58:23 and stayed elevated until 20:00:03. Width one runs first, so that window lands squarely on the sole temporal denominator: its 36 samples above 600 ms fall in rounds 46 to 93, its p95 is 1,674.197 ms and its maximum 3,192.573 ms, while widths 8, 16, 64 and 256 were measured after 20:00:03 on a quiet machine and have no sample above 600 ms at all. This is exactly the arbitrary in-block load change the adopted proposal said adjacency cannot remove, and it is why the 20-second load samples are evidence rather than housekeeping. They are going into the retained set beside the samples.\n\nThe verdict survives this, and I will show why rather than assert it. I computed the classification against four defensible width-one denominators: the full-block p50 of 471.761 ms, the full-block simple median of 474.324 ms, the first-quarter median of 448.474 ms taken from rounds 1 to 25 which fall entirely before the load event, and the last-quarter median of 735.251 ms which falls entirely inside it. PREVIEW and FIRST-PRODUCTION pass on all four. The worst case anywhere is width 8 at +3.566 percent against the pre-disturbance denominator, against a +10 percent limit. The magnitudes are denominator-sensitive and I will not publish them as if they were not; the classification is not.\n\nWHAT I WILL RETAIN, per the request. A tracked performance/retained set holding evidence.json, samples.jsonl, candidate.bench, the derived distributions, and notes recording exact head, contract and fixture digests, environment, the kill-and-restart history and the 20-second load samples. Excluded: the profiles directory the run also produced, traces, fixtures and anything carrying local paths or secrets. I will state the retained set's own digests in the notes so the files can be checked without trusting the page.\n\nI will not merge, and I will not amend a head once it is reviewed."}